WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.920
Does the Morningstar ever fade&nbsp;
away? In the case of Lucifer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.160
there's a strong chance the fallen&nbsp;
angel may stay gone for good.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.760
"Lucifer" may be centered on the literal&nbsp;
Devil, but it's not your average religious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:17.560
fantasy drama. The series does something unique,&nbsp;
mixing in elements of horror, mystery, thriller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.400
and police procedural, as Lucifer Morningstar&nbsp;
helps out on cases with the Los Angeles Police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.080
Department and runs a successful nightclub to&nbsp;
boot. Beside Lucifer is Detective Chloe Decker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.720
a dedicated cop who is somehow&nbsp;
immune to his manipulative powers.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.640
In addition to taking on the most grisly crimes,&nbsp;
Lucifer and Decker must contend with Decker's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.320
disgruntled ex-husband and fellow detective, Dan,&nbsp;
and Lucifer's brother Amenadiel. The angel wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.040
Lucifer to return back down below and will do&nbsp;
whatever it takes to get him back to ruling Hell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.080
To make things more complicated, though, Lucifer's&nbsp;
immortality seems to falter whenever Decker is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.360
near, making their already difficult partnership&nbsp;
all the more problematic when they fall in love.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.840
Over the course of the series, Amenadiel is joined&nbsp;
by his mother and the biblical Cain, among others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:07.560
who cause Earthly problems for Lucifer. But&nbsp;
when Decker discovers Lucifer's true face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.200
she struggles to accept that she's in love with&nbsp;
the Devil. In the show's final year, Lucifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.120
actually does the unthinkable, attempting to fill&nbsp;
the shoes of God himself while trying to rescue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:22.040
Dan who is trapped in Hell, all while trying to&nbsp;
find a new place for himself in the universe.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.960
It may be tempting to assume that "Lucifer"&nbsp;
was canceled due to lack of viewership or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.040
cost-cutting measures. But the truth&nbsp;
is, "Lucifer" ended on its own terms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.240
closing out its run by the decision of the series'&nbsp;
showrunners Joe Henderson and Ildy Modrovich,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.800
who knew when it was time to say goodbye. As&nbsp;
Henderson explained to Entertainment Weekly:

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.120
"It's the story we were always going to tell."

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.000
According to Henderson, the show was&nbsp;
almost going to end after Season 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.120
but it was actually Netflix who wanted them&nbsp;
to return for one more year. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:55.200
the story was split up into two seasons&nbsp;
of 16 and 10 episodes each. He said:

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.760
"What we realized is that the last bit of&nbsp;
that [series] finale episode was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.800
a lot of great stories sped up&nbsp;
just to give [it] a satisfying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.800
ending for all our [of] characters. We&nbsp;
literally lobbed off Act Six and went,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.360
'Let's take what happens in Act Six in a scene&nbsp;
and dive into it, and really explore how our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.800
characters end up where they ended up.' So,&nbsp;
that ended up being our nugget for Season 6."

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.160
In the end, though, the showrunners knew the&nbsp;
story was over, whether it was one season or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.920
two. They got to tell the story they wanted&nbsp;
and the series ended to their satisfaction.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.720
"So just think of me as your guardian devil."

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.080
"Lucifer" already said goodbye twice: in 2018&nbsp;
it was canceled after just three seasons on Fox,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.560
becoming a victim of poor ratings for a&nbsp;
prime-time series on a major network. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:43.800
Netflix swooped in and rescued the series, giving&nbsp;
it three more seasons and 36 additional episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.760
much to the delight of fans. But&nbsp;
since it bid farewell in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.480
there hasn't been so much as a peep&nbsp;
regarding a return for Season 7.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.680
As it stands, the sixth season finale was&nbsp;
a fitting end for Lucifer and the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.480
as a whole. It ended with Lucifer becoming a&nbsp;
therapist, and the credits rolled after a brief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.560
reunion when Decker entered his office.&nbsp;
As the show's co-showrunners have said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.360
this was the perfect farewell, and the&nbsp;
lack of a seventh season at this point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:12.840
is really no mystery. The people behind the&nbsp;
show simply don't seem all that interested in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.440
bringing the cast back for more when it's so&nbsp;
fresh from having ended its phenomenal run.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.480
Still, considering the series&nbsp;
has already survived one ending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.360
it could live to see another season. Revivals&nbsp;
after years off the air are nothing new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:29.120
and shows like "Good Omens" and "American&nbsp;
Gods" have proven there's a thriving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.520
appetite for offbeat stories about&nbsp;
biblical angels and demons on Earth.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.800
The cast of "Lucifer" went through a number&nbsp;
of changes during its six seasons on the air.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.440
While Tom Ellis and Lauren German headlined the&nbsp;
series for its entire run as Lucifer and Decker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:47.960
respectively, several others came and went.&nbsp;
For example, Kevin Alejandro, D.B. Woodside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.240
and Lesley-Ann Brandt made it through&nbsp;
all six seasons as Detective Espinoza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:58.120
Amenadiel, and the demon Mazikeen, but Kevin&nbsp;
Rankin was long gone by Season 6. The likes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.800
Tom Welling and Tricia Helfer both were at one&nbsp;
point series regulars midway through the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.040
while Brianna Hildebrand was added&nbsp;
to the show in its final year.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.760
If "Lucifer" is to be taken seriously&nbsp;
in a potential seventh season, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.840
Ellis and German will have to reprise their&nbsp;
roles at the very least. It's also possible that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:19.280
Alejandro and Helfer could return, given how their&nbsp;
story was left at the end of Season 6. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.400
Brandt may not necessarily need to come&nbsp;
back, but she could receive her own spin-off.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.520
While it's likely that a Season 7 would bring&nbsp;
back most of the show's roster of stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.840
it wouldn't be hard to imagine some new actors&nbsp;
joining the ensemble. Whether that's a new demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.520
or angel, or even another fellow detective,&nbsp;
there's plenty of room for some fresh talent.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.640
"You scared I'm turning my&nbsp;
back on the dark side, bro?"

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:43.320
There's plenty to speculate on given where&nbsp;
the finale left all of its characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.360
including Lucifer himself.&nbsp;
In the final installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:50.240
we see him having entirely abandoned&nbsp;
both his duties as ruler of Hell and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.680
his temporary position as God, which is now&nbsp;
being performed by his brother Amenadiel.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.160
A potential angle for a continuation&nbsp;
might be to flip the premise on its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.080
head by ditching the police procedural&nbsp;
format entirely and turning the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.800
into more of a medical procedural. Given the&nbsp;
producers' desire to end the series as it was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.120
it stands to reason they'd be looking for&nbsp;
a fresh approach if they were to bring it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.240
back. The notion of the Devil incarnate serving&nbsp;
as counsel to patients struggling with their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.360
mental health could be just the kind of new&nbsp;
idea to allow the show to continue. And with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:23.320
his vast experiences on Earth and beyond, who&nbsp;
better to listen and offer advice than Lucifer?

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:28.000
Similarly, the new roles for the supporting cast&nbsp;
offer plenty of opportunity for continuation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.480
with Mazikeen and Eve now romantically&nbsp;
involved and serving as villain hunters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:35.320
themselves. Meanwhile, the continuation of&nbsp;
the family line in the form of Amenadiel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.720
son Charlie could see a new&nbsp;
young demon join the cast.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.640
The cast of "Lucifer" has been mum&nbsp;
on their interest in returning for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.560
the series to date. While the showrunners&nbsp;
were happy with how the series concluded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.800
they have added further commentary since&nbsp;
then. A year after the series concluded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.200
they seemed at least somewhat open to thinking&nbsp;
about a future for the show. Coinciding with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.400
the release of "Lucifer" on home media, they&nbsp;
sat down for an interview with Screen Rant in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:04.200
September 2022, where they were asked about the&nbsp;
possibility of another go. Joe Henderson said:

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:09.400
"I mean, I hope so. We loved making the show,&nbsp;
we loved working with these people. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:14.360
hopefully at some point, we can find a way to&nbsp;
come back, or at least revisit or do something."

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.120
Whether that means another full season,&nbsp;
a single streaming movie, or a spin-off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:22.360
it sounds like Henderson is most excited&nbsp;
about reuniting with his cast and crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.040
no matter what form it takes. He admitted&nbsp;
how the whole experience turned out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:30.640
be so wonderful along with the people, so he&nbsp;
wouldn't write off the possibility entirely.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.920
Of course, Ildy Modrovich&nbsp;
couldn't resist the chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.800
to slip in a somewhat sly response. She said:

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.200
"My vote is for 'Lucifer The&nbsp;
Musical,' personally, on Broadway."

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.840
Henderson followed up immediately with&nbsp;
the sarcastic suggestion of "Lucifer:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.360
The Animated Series."

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.160
"Chloe, is my chin…"

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:46.880
"Buttlike?"

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.040
"I was gonna say this amazing in real life."

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:54.080
Sure, what fans really want to see is another&nbsp;
full season of "Lucifer," or perhaps a full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:59.120
movie that directly follows Season 6 of the show.&nbsp;
That being said, there may be opportunities for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.880
Tom Ellis to reprise his title role somewhere&nbsp;
other than a traditional revival. For starters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:08.520
he's already turned up in a cameo in The&nbsp;
CW's "Crisis on Infinite Earths" storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:12.880
that included Tyler Hoechlin's Superman. Is it&nbsp;
possible we could see Lucifer back in action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.560
in Hoechlin's "Superman &amp; Lois"? It may seem&nbsp;
like a long shot, but it's certainly possible.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:21.840
James Gunn is assembling an all-new DC&nbsp;
universe of films. Though much of it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.880
expected to be entirely new, he's not averse&nbsp;
to bringing in existing characters and actors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.600
as evidenced by the return of his "Peacemaker"&nbsp;
cast. So far, he hasn't recruited anyone from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:36.320
the vast universe of television shows, but&nbsp;
it's certainly not a hard-and-fast rule,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.800
and we've seen rival Marvel do that very thing&nbsp;
when they brought Charlie Cox into the MCU.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:45.920
With Gunn's initial "Gods and Monsters" phase of&nbsp;
the new DCU putting an emphasis on the bizarre,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.400
it could very well require a devil to oversee&nbsp;
the spiritual side of things. If it does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.640
Gunn could recruit Ellis to&nbsp;
fill that role as Lucifer.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:57.800
Fans of "Lucifer" have proven just how dedicated&nbsp;
they are to their favorite series. It was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:02.680
fan-driven effort that got the series back from&nbsp;
the brink of extinction in 2018 when it was axed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:07.720
by Fox. Banding together as only fans can,&nbsp;
they started a "Save Lucifer" campaign that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:12.400
burned up social media and forced Hollywood&nbsp;
to take notice. Eventually, that passionate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.440
outpouring of fan support convinced Netflix to&nbsp;
take a leap of faith and bring the series back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.160
which ultimately led to three successful follow-up&nbsp;
seasons. Flash forward to the show's conclusion on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.600
streaming, and the fans were back at it hoping&nbsp;
to convince the powers-that-be to do it again.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.120
Fans rallied on Change.org the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:35.160
with a petition that garnered in excess of&nbsp;
300,000 signatures to save the show. In 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:41.120
fans once again gained more than 119,000-plus&nbsp;
supporters to get the show a sixth season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.240
And while several current petitions on the&nbsp;
site have yet to crack those lofty figures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:49.200
their repeated appearance is proof enough&nbsp;
that fans of the show aren't to be overlooked.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.040
A petition to bring Lucifer and Decker back&nbsp;
for "Lucifer: The Movie" has amassed several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.080
thousand signatures, too. These are sure to&nbsp;
be numbers that Netflix is paying attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:02.400
to. Needless to say, if there ever is going&nbsp;
to be a Season 7 or continuation of any sort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.680
it will be the fans of the show who will likely&nbsp;
be playing a role in helping make it happen.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:10.200
"Devil bunnies. Oh no. Luci-fans."

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.560
If there is ever going to be a Season&nbsp;
7 of "Lucifer," there is a way that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:17.600
could happen. Though the two showrunners have&nbsp;
jokingly responded to questions with offers of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:22.440
a musical and an animated series, they also seem&nbsp;
genuinely interested in revisiting the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.920
at some point down the line. With streaming&nbsp;
services also struggling in recent times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:31.080
the need for established hits could see Tom&nbsp;
Ellis pulled back into his popular role.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.200
That's not the only way we could see a new season,&nbsp;
though. There's also the possibility that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:40.200
further adventures of Lucifer Morningstar could&nbsp;
be explored outside of live-action TV. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:44.520
it was a sarcastic comment at the time, Joe&nbsp;
Henderson's suggestion of an animated offering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:49.680
might be a legitimate possibility. After all,&nbsp;
the classic 1960s "Batman" series got a pair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.800
of animated movie sequels, and there's long been&nbsp;
talk of an animated "Smallville" follow-up. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.800 --> 00:10:00.280
the show featured an animated episode in&nbsp;
Season 6, showing that the format is doable.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.640
"Oh, that's absurd. And his chin&nbsp;
definitely looks like a butt."

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.800
Another possibility with some merit&nbsp;
could be turning a potential Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:12.720
7 into a comic book sequel series, bringing&nbsp;
the show back to its source material medium.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:16.880
From "Buffy the Vampire Slayer" to "The&nbsp;
X-Files" and "Smallville," a number of hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:21.320
shows have given fans additional "seasons"&nbsp;
in comic book form. In the case of "X-Men:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:27.143
The Animated Series," the comic book sequel "X-Men&nbsp;
'92" even led to a revival of the show itself.

